<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jizya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jizya was a tax levied in Islamic states on non-Muslim subjects, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhimmi">dhimmi</a>, in return for protection and exemption from military service. It was established in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> and continued in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>, where it was an important source of revenue. It was also collected in later states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
